File: wave.info, Node: mirror, Next: latest, Prev: linkquery, Up: Top


Show the address each kind of data is fetched from, including the
built-in defaults for anything not overridden by an environment
variable.

  --json
      Print the configuration as JSON

  --yaml
      Print the configuration as YAML

  --toml
      Print the configuration as TOML

  --raw
      Print ready-to-paste export lines

  --only-set
      With --raw: export only the sources you overrode, leaving the rest
      to follow the built-in defaults

  --show-password
      Print passwords in full instead of six asterisks

  --hide-user
      Also mask the user name

Examples:

     wave mirror
     wave mirror --raw
     wave mirror --json
     wave mirror --show-password


File: wave.info, Node: latest, Next: shellenv, Prev: mirror, Up: Top


Compare what you have with the newest version in the index. Reports
only; nothing is downloaded.

  -a, --all
      Check every installed package

  --max-time <string>
      Total time limit for each request (e.g. 40s, 1min)

  --connect-timeout <string>
      Give up if the handshake takes longer

  --content-time <string>
      Give up if no data arrives for this long

  -v, --verbose
      Print each request as it is made

Examples:

     wave latest jq
     wave latest --all
     wave latest -a --max-time=1min


